{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 5.591, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11267, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 869, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01HmJtnGCrKq1BQek5BYiHD4", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses a one-sided threshold: 2Δln L = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71) from the likelihood maximum. It profiles over the individual dwarfs' J-factors, using a Gaussian prior on log10 of the J-factor normalization. The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = Δ(−2 ln L) = 3.84, the nominal one-parameter 95% interval, and reports its upper endpoint. The paper says this differs from the usual one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197) and a range of 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T080550Z_dev-02_staged_f742", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses a one-sided threshold: 2Δln L = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71) from the likelihood maximum. It profiles over the individual dwarfs' J-factors, using a Gaussian prior on log10 of the J-factor normalization. The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = Δ(−2 ln L) = 3.84, the nominal one-parameter 95% interval, and reports its upper endpoint. The paper says this differs from the usual one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197) and a range of 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 10.337, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19594, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1188, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 26627, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T08:06:01+00:00"}
